MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Beach Boys and the Righteous Brothers feel like natural next choices because their melodies and vocal harmonies connect with my Beatles, Simon & Garfunkel, and mid-sixties listening.",
    "Jim Croce and Peter, Paul and Mary fit the acoustic storytelling and close harmonies I enjoy in Jonathan Edwards, Melanie, and Simon & Garfunkel; Eagles also fits my interest in melodic classic rock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Toby Keith's collection does not follow the older pop, folk, and classic-rock sound I want right now; being another greatest-hits collection is not enough to make it appealing.",
    "Queen and Journey fit my broader interests, but their bigger rock anthems appeal less today than gentler songs. I also cannot judge The Complete Hit Singles without knowing the artist."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been treated as a preference that carries across artists, when the songs and sound matter more than the collection format.",
    "My classic-rock listening seems to have been interpreted broadly, although melodic rock, acoustic folk, and arena-rock anthems do not feel equally appealing to me today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My listening to Melanie, Jonathan Edwards, and Simon & Garfunkel points toward gentle vocals, acoustic storytelling, and close harmonies that make certain choices especially appealing.",
    "A collection can match my general taste without being something I would choose now: ELO fits, for example, but the folk and sixties-pop selections draw me more strongly today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar melodic music, but gave too much weight to greatest-hits collections and broad classic-rock connections over my current preference for gentler folk and sixties harmonies."
}
